    question: 'The Mongol invasions of Japan in 1274 and 1281 CE were repelled partly by storms the Japanese called what?',
    options: ['Kamikaze (Divine Wind)', 'Oni (Demon Storm)', 'Raijin\'s Fury', 'Fujin\'s Breath'],
    correctIndex: 0,
    explanation: 'Typhoons struck the Mongol fleets in both 1274 and 1281, destroying much of the invading forces. Japanese defenders called these storms "kamikaze" (divine wind), believing the gods had protected Japan from conquest.',
